0 FILE stud4s.dat
0 Stud Tube Open Sloped
0 Name: stud4s.dat
0 Author: Willy Tschager [Holly-Wood]
0 !LDRAW_ORG Primitive UPDATE 2024-01
0 !LICENSE Licensed under CC BY 4.0 : see CAreadme.txt

0 !HELP For use between a stud4a and a sloped surface. It is enough
0 !HELP to know coordinates Y of the centre and that of the outside
0 !HELP circle. The difference of both coordinates is the height of
0 !HELP the primitive to be applied. Finally, this primitive can be
0 !HELP used with all the parts sloped using a STUD4A. H = Y center
0 !HELP sloped - Y common border.

0 BFC CERTIFY CCW

0 !HISTORY 2009-09-03 [PTadmin] Official Update 2009-02
0 !HISTORY 2024-01-18 [Holly-Wood] Complete rewrite, original by guyvivan
0 !HISTORY 2024-01-29 [OrionP] Official Update 2024-01

0 // Edges
1 16 0 -1 0 6 0 0 0.75 1 0 0 0 6 4-4edge.dat
1 16 0 -1 0 8 0 0 1 1 0 0 0 8 4-4edge.dat

0 // Faces
0 BFC INVERTNEXT
1 16 0 0 0 6 0 0 0 -0.25 0 0 0 6 4-4cyli.dat
0 BFC INVERTNEXT
1 16 0 -0.25 0 6 0 0 0 -0.75 0 0 0 6 4-4cyls.dat
1 16 0 0 0 8 0 0 0 -1 0 0 0 8 4-4cyls.dat


